6. This order shall remain operative subject to compliance of the following conditions by the applicant:-
(i) The applicant shall comply with all the terms and conditions of the bond executed by him;
(ii) The applicant shall cooperate in the investigation/trial, as the case may be;
(iii) The applicant shall not indulge himself in extending inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade them from disclosing such facts to the Court or to the Police Officer, as the case may be;
(iv) The applicant shall not commit an offence similar to the offence of which he is accused;
(v). The applicant shall not seek unnecessary adjournments during the trial;
(vi) The applicant shall not leave India without previous permission of the trial Court/Investigating Officer, as the case may be;
( vii) The applicant would not be a source of embarrassment or harassment to the prosecutrix in any manner and shall not move in her vicinity and shall not try to contact the prosecutrix in person Shekh Subham Mansuri vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 17 February, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/153381325/
2 through electronic mode or through somebody else (viii) The applicant shall mark his presence on every Sunday and Thursday of every month before the police station concerned between 10:30 a.m. and 2:30 p.m. till filing of the charge-sheet.

